        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric of silk satin, woven by Daniel Walters & Sons, Spitalfields, London, 1870s"@en , "Furnishing fabric of silk twill satin. With a repeating formal pattern of symmetrical stems and scrolling leaf forms, topped by a flower and three cinquefoil leaves, in white silk on blue. The pattern is bound in twill on a satin ground."@en ;
